## DryRun mocks use silent defaults (may mask missing resource wiring)

Mock values for resources default to deterministic values:
  - Platform::Linux
  - Timestamp(0)
  - EnvVars empty map

This is good for determinism but acts as a fallback — a DAG can appear
to work in DryRun even if it never properly acquired/wired those resources.

**Suggested fix:** Consider a "strict DryRun" mode where env-node outputs
default to poison/UNSET unless explicitly mocked. Missing resource wiring
would then fail loudly instead of silently working with defaults.

